    "reason": "While '機関' can mean 'system' (Sense 2 in JMdict), it often carries more specific connotations of 'engine', 'agency', 'organization', or 'facility'. It does not cover the full breadth of the general English lemma 'system', which can refer to abstract frameworks, methods, or interconnected parts without a strong physical or organizational implication. For a general learner, '機関' is not the most natural or common translation for the broad concept of 'system'. Other Japanese terms like 'システム' (katakana), '制度' (for social/institutional systems), or '体系' (for structured systems/frameworks) are often more appropriate depending on context. For a general 'system', 'システム' is the most natural and broadly applicable choice.",
